// Composition of two stdlib library macros: `bind` takes the aggregation
// macro `count_within` as its value argument. Before the arg-classification
// fix, a bare aggregation-macro call in an argument position parsed as a
// condition and was rejected; it now expands to a `Term::Agg` and fills the
// comparison-operand slot (`?A == ?n`).
//
// Permit an Alert only when more than two Logins to the same server have
// occurred within the last hour. Verdict-equivalent to the hand-written
// `exists (n: Long). ((count for (t). where (…)) == n && n > 2)` form.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    bind(c, count_within(1h, Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: _, input.server: context.input.server }), c > 2)
};
